{"title":"2010 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tony works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours a day and is paid &#36;<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa10fc328b191089b850fd630e4c04747653da00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> per hour for each full year of his age. During a six month period Tony worked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days and earned &#36;<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a9644fb50e7a7520c3046182fe4c6e6adc11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. How old was Tony at the end of the six month period?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e40887bcacbbc9aa999041ddd50e9009c17b06d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"379\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tony works <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours a day and is paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa10fc328b191089b850fd630e4c04747653da00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> dollars per hour for each full year of his age. This basically says that he gets a dollar for each year of his age. So if he is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> years old, he gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollars a day. We also know that he worked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days and earned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a9644fb50e7a7520c3046182fe4c6e6adc11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> dollars. If he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> years old at the beginning of his working period, he would have earned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a4708d47c30ad7b2a5939e039cdfccc1ac9da690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 * 50 = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> dollars. If he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> years old at the beginning of his working period, he would have earned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a19b6a004bcaeb48badb4a5af73fb1b53cf2ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 * 50 = 650$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> dollars. Because he earned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a9644fb50e7a7520c3046182fe4c6e6adc11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> dollars, we know that he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for some period of time, but not the whole time, because then the money earned would be greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/12060badf8be82c1d7ae05f240e571d68f73ddfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$650$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. This is why he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> when he began, but turned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sometime during the six month period and earned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a9644fb50e7a7520c3046182fe4c6e6adc11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> dollars in total. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />. We could find out for how long he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f7562cdc646f661f79785c66ba2d32fdc0af3df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot x + 13 \\cdot (50-x) = 630$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and we know that he was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equal Tony's age at the end of the period. We know that his age changed during the time period (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a9644fb50e7a7520c3046182fe4c6e6adc11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> does not evenly divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />). Thus, his age at the beginning of the time period is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b0495af1d7b094561fcade343847d464778c925d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of days Tony worked while his age was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. We know that his earnings every day equal his age (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3c5a19c906e25bba9cf2b759682a11739f96f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 0.50 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" />). Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c26a9949828947c54a73b4373bb229cb19b5c09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\cdot d + (x - 1)(50 - d) = 630\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/845d1bcd6fa794739291be04cf262f8c0cab48ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\cdot d + 50x - x\\cdot d - 50 + d = 630\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a3e43583ccd6a7d893f4ed92346e54c8670dce0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[50x + d = 680\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/3440645b3bb386d007d6362b8eee6333f7dd2eed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\dfrac{680 - d}{50}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210e79232fe84e26bc1ead08cd41206370f3e7dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; d &lt;50$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1dacac204a1ac6c9a81ae3277ced90ccbaa5a4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 30$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. Then we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa808b493f01f66b0bfdeb7ab0ab4f85d8c3e468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50x = 650$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e5b2ed0c958e21e728ed4d11539179bdbc8eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{(D) 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"94\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Tony worked for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> days, he has worked for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> hours. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be his hourly wage. Then, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/2466dbff7735c257f244386761bfecbda4b977ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100k = 630$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />(Daily wage, which is equal to his age) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc54ef8feabfc5d0a2329f0cfbd10af8a6a809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\approx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f9f10489f5c393568d444e1fab55c655a98f53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12.6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />. Since we now know that his age was either 12 or 13 during the 6 month span, and we are asked to find his age at the end of this time, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e03ea24ebe7ef7a0073ab912955227fef362069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D) 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/P7rGLXp_6es?t=244\">https://youtu.be/P7rGLXp_6es?t=244</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\"